  "summary": "When You Look Up passes for an adult parish because \u201cThe man speaking to them is the one who will come in the cloud\u201d explains why the disciples can lift their heads, and Paul's warning about contention and the Gradual's petition earn the invitation to repair a neighbor's welcome. I checked the spoken body and note against the study, the 1962 Missal pp. [1]\u20132, Challoner\u2019s Lk 21, Rom 13 and Pss 24 and 84, Gregory I.1 \u00a7\u00a71\u20135, Chrysostom on Romans, Homily 24, and Augustine on Ps 84 \u00a7\u00a710 and 12, and confirmed with TeXcount that the body has 1,172 spoken words, an estimated 10.2\u201311.2 minutes at 105\u2013115 words per minute."
